{nicte ze'ei co'o} doesn't even really make sense if you ignore English; it
means "night", the predicate, but has the grammar of selma'o COI. That is,
the semantics of the second word are completely ignored, only its grammar is
significant.

Personally I'd just say {co'o xamgu sipna} or something, I think.

mu'o mi'e .latros.

